+
+Multer validation requiring file bytes necessarily follows admission. Authentication precedes protected parsers; new uploads have no caller-selected foreign object to authorize. Existing commit fences independently recheck ownership/account state after an intervening storage PUT. JSON is bounded globally; contact role/message shape is now rejected before charging its low-frequency quotas. Invalid/missing recipient and SMTP failure still consume prior admission, matching the conservative existing policy.
+
+## Whole-application Redis audit / responsibility matrix
+
+The endpoint appendix lists every mounted declaration, including router-wide authentication/roles/organization guards. The following branches are unchanged unless explicitly marked migrated. A service import alone does not prove a Redis command executes on every request.
